t":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T13:43:24-08:00","id":1547555,"title":"","content":"I see that you borrowed a element of what Gesu did to Lilian in the dark ages. He embraced her and made her part of his body with her face visible on his chest. Much to the torment of his brother Symeon who had strong strong feelings for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T17:37:52-08:00","id":1547566,"title":"","content":"I actually didn't know about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T22:00:54-08:00","id":1547570,"title":"","content":"It's was part of the Constantinople by Night sourcebook when they covered the Tziscme faction led by Dracon's childe Gesu. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T19:05:58-07:00","id":1552639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1547344#post1547344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her Attributes are low for a Sixth Generation vampire and she only has one Background. She has a lot of really good Disciplines, but you don\u2019t tell us how many dots she has in each Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>She would have her diciplines of atleast 5 or more with her Vicissitude being 9 or 10 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-25T03:10:04-07:00","id":1552644,"title":"","content":"As a four-armed muscular giantess almost 5 meters high, it would make more sense for her to have at least Strength 6. Higher Perception due to the 8 eyes would also make sense. An elder isn't just high Discipline dots, and actually being very high on every Discipline doesn't make a lot of sense, nor keeping other traits low compensate for it.<br /> <br /> How would her Vicissitude be 9/10 dots at 6th Generation? Her trait limit is 7. Maybe she has more than one Elder Power at 6th and 7th levels, but not more actual dots.<br /> <br /> You may decide she achieved Golconda, but that seems pretty off. What's the role/purpose of this character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T18:56:10-07:00","id":1552664,"title":"","content":"I thought you had to be at least 6th to get higher than 5 dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T20:55:24-07:00","id":1552668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1552664#post1552664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought you had to be at least 6th to get higher than 5 dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>7th.<br /> <br /> Each Generation bellow 8th adds 1 to your trait limits. This limit is the same for Attributes, Abilities and Disciplines. You only get to raise things up to 10 without being 3rd Gen if you reach Golconda (although you still have to pay the XP cost).<br /> <br /> As a 6th Gen Koldun, she may have up to 7 at any such traits, and it's likely that she'll have at least 6 in some <b>if she's an Elder</b>, which you didn't sated, did you?<br /> <br /> Talking about NPCs, the best approach (for verissimilitude under normal circumstances, which is but one aspect of their design) is for their traits to accompany their age. Neonates are unlikely to have any trait at all above 5 (and in fact to have anything at 5), regardless of their Generation. Elders are usually the ones to have reached the limits afforded by their Generation.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are a special case, because at the same time that they're trained, they're by design the hardest thing to raise. It's unlikely that a given character will have more Disciplines at their peak level than other traits, even because they usually need better dice pools more than new powers (especially at the rather lackluster elder leves).<br /> <br /> Other than that, try to have a distribution between high level and low level powers. A character with 11 Disciplines, every single one of them at 5+ is very weird, specially if the rest of the sheet does not follow. There's nothing wrong with an elder having a few Disciplines at levels 1-3.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you have a particular story or role that requires her traits as they are. This character remains without context, and without context it's hard to evaluate anything about her. You don't need to have a game where to really use her, but you do need to have a general idea of what kind of story you want to tell with her in your head, or what kind of use you would like to make of her in an ideal world, even if it is a world that'll never come true. The exercise is always welcome, but the character still has to have a context in this exercise to make any particular sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T11:58:56-07:00","id":1552724,"title":"","content":"Well, she's an Elder of course and has existed since the Dark Ages if her last name is anything to go by. I just felt that making her a 4th generation methuselah would be a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 07-29-2025, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T18:56:13-07:00","id":1553019,"title":"","content":"The role of the NPC is to be someone like Andrei from Bloodlines who is hard to kill and keeps coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T18:03:17-07:00","id":1553049,"title":"","content":"Would it be better to make her a Methuselah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T18:11:54-07:00","id":1553051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553049#post1553049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be better to make her a Methuselah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, without context it's impossible to say.<br /> <br /> Being hard to kill is how she's supposed to work as a stat block, but not what she does.<br /> <br /> What is her purpose? Without this, the question is nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T06:12:33-07:00","id":1553058,"title":"","content":"What I meant was they're going to be an antagonist that keeps coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T06:42:33-07:00","id":1553059,"title":"","content":"Regardless of the Era you play, it not have to be a Methuselah or even an Elder<br /> A recurring enemy could be in their age range, heck, even younger - that makes it more scary<br /> It is just realyl the right amount of connections and resoruces and the survability of a cockroach (with Flaws and merits like 9 lives) <br /> Someone who could be their friend, the member of their coteria is way more devastating on the moral level than an eldrich horror-like Elder<br /> It also gives hope, because anyone one of them could be that enemy, they just need an opportunity... and to let go certain morals and self erected walls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T11:02:53-07:00","id":1553068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553058#post1553058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was they're going to be an antagonist that keeps coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a normal game, 4th Gen is too much, 6th is already quite good.<br /> <br /> Focus on <b>Fortitude</b> and <b>Vicissitude</b>, things that'll make her resilient without making her too much of an immediate threat (otherwise she'll just wipe the PCs). A couple dots in <b>Auspex</b> are enough to justify her noticing danger soon enough to be prepared (which is the most important survival strategy). <b>Celerity</b> is good, but don't overdo it, just enough to keep defensive and flee when the shit hits the fan.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it depends a lot on how she'll antagonize the PCs. <b>Koldunic Sorcery</b> is a good choice to have high as it makes for variety and for her primary concept, but the others depend a lot. I see a number of Disciplines there that have little reason to be there other than accumulating powers. If they have just 1 or 2 dots each, this is interesting as someone who's a dabbler in every &quot;magic&quot; available, but otherwise it'll just make her harder to use for no payback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T14:41:07-07:00","id":1553074,"title":"","content":"Well, the reason she has stuff like Necromancy and Protean is because she's a Metamorphosist trying to understand the vampiric condition. Most of the other Disciplines are for survival and staying hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-11-2025, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T18:38:30-07:00","id":1553078,"title":"","content":"That counts as a dabbler, thematically speaking. And with the exception of very specific Paths, <b>Necromancy</b> won't really help her studies. And as a sorcery Discipline, it begs the question of how she studied it.<br /> <br /> But it's still unclear how she'll antagonize the PCs. What she does, like, what are her activities and business right now? How she gets stuff done? What kinds of connections, mundane resources and obligations she has, beyond what's in the stat block?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T19:54:53-07:00","id":1553080,"title":"","content":"Well, she has a few bloodbound revenants which help her do business and her stat block indicates that she understands a lot about medicine, surgery and spiking blood with drugs and poisons. She practiced a lot of Diablerie to get as good as she is in Disciplines. She also has a sufficient understanding of the Supernatural including Werewolves, Wraiths, Changelings, etc. She has access to businesses and slave networks via her revenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-11-2025, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T00:05:16-07:00","id":1553083,"title":"","content":"To elaborate a bit on what (I think) <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is trying to get at, it seems like the problem is that you're thinking about this character more as a plot device than as a character.<br /> <br /> You seem to have a few basic ideas about their motivations and opinions, but most of what you have been telling us so far involves superficial details about her abilities and appearance. But to build an antagonist, those things are actually less important than their relationship with the PCs.<br /> <br /> *Why* does this 15-foot-tall monstrous muscle-mommy care about the PCs, or why do they care about *her*?<br /> <br /> It's hard to know what kinds of stats are particularly appropriate for an antagonist to have without knowing the nature of their conflict with the PCs. This is less important if you're just trying to make a cool NPC who just exists in the background of your setting, who your players may never even meet if they don't feel like doing so. They're just flavour. But if you specifically want someone to be an *antagonist*, you need to start by considering the source of their conflict with the PCs, and build out from there. Once you've figured out the nature of that conflict, then you can start determining what abilities (skills, Disciplines, etc.) are needed to fulfill that function.<br /> <br /> Looking to motivations a bit more generally, it's worth homing in a bit on the fact that the NPC is supposed to be a Metamorphosist. While pursuing Metamorphosis involves studying of the vampire condition, those studies have to be directed towards the &quot;perfection&quot; of the vampire condition. And it really helps to have some idea of what your Metamorphosist N/PC has in mind when they think of &quot;perfection.&quot; This matters because there should presumably be an underlying rationale behind the abilities and Disciplines the characters will pursue, along with the modifications that she chooses to make to her body. In the Dark Ages, there was (in DAV20, at least) a split within the Road of Metamorphosis between the &quot;Path of Flesh&quot; and &quot;Path of Spirit,&quot; which place different amounts of emphasis on physical versus spiritual transformation. The former is probably more likely to focus on physical Disciplines and stuff like Protean in addition to Vicissitude, while the latter would probably be more likely to supplement their Vicissitude with spiritual practices like Koldunism or other forms of blood magic. And then you have other practices like those of the Exsanguinists that, depending on how you look at it, could line up with either branch. All of which is to say that you have to spend some time thinking about your antagonist's approach to Metamorphosis before you can decide what Disciplines, etc., are going to be their top priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T04:34:49-07:00","id":1553085,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> got it. I wouldn't even say just as a plot device, but more specifically you're still thinking about this character as a stat block, and the story just as a justification for said stats, when it should be the other way around.<br /> <br /> What's the story of this character? What's the conflict? Why should the PCs care? How will they interact? Which kinds of scenes you picture her in? What is she trying to accomplish, and what are you trying to accomplish with her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T08:08:02-07:00","id":1553093,"title":"","content":"Well, since she's a member of the Sabbat the characters will likely come into conflict with her. She's been around since the Dark Ages and she subsumed her lovers so they could never leave her. She might kidnap someone affiliated with the Coterie which could lead to conflict. Her goal is of course to achieve Azhi Dahaka by any means necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T09:34:23-07:00","id":1553098,"title":"","content":"On my phone, so just firing off a couple of points quickly:<br /> <br /> 1) Her being a member of the Sabbat does not guarantee a conflict with the PCs. For that to be the case, both her and the PCs would need to be on the &quot;front lines&quot; of some battle between the Sects. Where is it? How long has the fighting been going on? Where is muscle-mommy's place in all this? It's important to consider that most Metamorphosists don't really give a damn about Sabbat politics, so if she's getting involved, there has to be a good reason.<br /> <br /> 2) What is Azhi Dahaka? Ask ten Metamorphosists, and you'll probably get at least 10 answers, quite possibly more. This is why I spent a bunch of time rambling about the Path in my previous post. Without knowing what her particular notion of perfection or transcendance is, many of the skills or Disciplines you want to give her could be a pointless dead end.<br /> <br /> Yorak is considered one of the greatest Metamorphosists to ever exist, and they (probably) didn't have any dots in Necromancy. So why does your Tzimisce think that it's worth the time and trouble? I can think of at least two answers to that question, but which one you pick is going to depend on the specific approach that your character follows in pursuing Azhi Dahaka. And you would choose different Necromancy Paths depending on that approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T10:56:58-07:00","id":1553100,"title":"","content":"Her idea of Azhi Dahaka is both physical and spiritual transcendance. A conflict could be in her haven which is an abandoned mall with all the glass (Windows, doors, etc.) having been replaced with wood and sheet metal. While the inside is filled with bodies on examination tables in varying states of dismemberment and fleshcrafted architecture and a room with soil from her homeland. The haven is guarded by Zantosa and Grimaldi Revenants with flamethrowers, maybe some Enrathi or Rafastio, Szlachta, Hellhounds, a Vozhd, zombies, wraiths and a pack of bloodbrothers. For an Elder as experienced and skilled as she is it would make sense to make her haven a Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-12-2025, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T10:59:21-07:00","id":1553101,"title":"","content":"We're not asking questions to validate or not your character concept. You don't need that, the character is valid by itself.<br /> <br /> The questions are meant for you to engage with them, because complete, pondered answers will help us help you. If you keep giving short answers without engaging them, we can't do much more for you here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:08:10-07:00","id":1553103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553100#post1553100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Elder as experienced and skilled as she is it would make sense to make her haven a Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. If she's someone who'll be tough to kill and frequently flee to fight another day, she may have a haven that's easy to replace, so she can flee and reestablish herself elsewhere. Or it may be a gauntlet, but then it would be the place of her last-ish battle, which would imply she's highly active outside, engaging with the PCs somewhere else for several stories before being cornered in her haven.<br /> <br /> Also, it's possible that the chronicle itself takes place at her homeland, so bringing soil isn't a concern. Especially if she has <b>Animalism</b> and <b>Koldunic Sorcery</b>, the Tzimisce benefit a lot from being sedentary and integrating with their Domain, in whatever sense they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:12:53-07:00","id":1553104,"title":"","content":"Maybe the reason the coterie came into conflict with her in the first place is because she stole artifacts from them or kidnapped someone they knew for some purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:53:03-07:00","id":1553108,"title":"","content":"If you want a recurrent villan, rather than doing one dastardly action, I think it could be better if her long term goals are somehow opposed to the long term goals of your players.<br /> <br /> I.E: if your players want to become the prince/authorities of the Camarilla, then her being (or obeying) an authority of the Sabbat that wants to expand the influence of the sect over the same territory it's going to end being a thorn in their asses at some point, organically.<br /> <hr />Also, let's remember the old ST mantra:<br /> <br /> No plan ever survives encounter with the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T12:07:45-07:00","id":1553110,"title":"","content":"What artifacts, and why?<br /> <br /> Why kidnap that particular person?<br /> <br /> These are the kind of details we're looking to have explained, and your responses up to now have seemed mostly to just brush them off as unimportant, when they are actually *the* most important thing.<br /> <br /> Another point worth mentioning is that it's important to consider the PCs themselves. If you're going to start a conflict by kidnapping an NPC, you need to make sure that they *care* about that NPC.<br /> <br /> It'd be a little awkward if you tell the players &quot;oh no, your friendly neighbourhoid Thaumaturge John has gone missing, it looks like he's been kidnapped&quot; and they respond &quot;ok, I guess we'll start making introductions to the Banu Haqim ashipu up the street.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T15:13:29-07:00","id":1553113,"title":"","content":"Because I don't have a coterie I'm just putting out a concept for an NPC and want an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-12-2025, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T16:32:44-07:00","id":1553114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553113#post1553113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I don't have a coterie I'm just putting out a concept for an NPC and want an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> made a good point that a more structural and ongoing source of potential conflict might work better than a single inciting incident, especially if you don't have a specific group of PCs in mind that said incident could be tailored to. While I said earlier that you should keep in mind that Metamorphosists don't really care about Sect politics, that wasn't meant to say that's a bad idea, but just that you need to think through the reason why she would bother getting involved. If she's taking on the role of a war leader, it could provide the opportunity to raid for test subjects while shoring up her relationship with the Sect. If she's been given the job of defending an area under Sabbat control, it gives her the opportunity to take advantage of the Tzimisce predilection for controlling territory that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> mentioned earlier, *especially* as a Koldun; the Way of Spirit is really good at helping to keep an eye on, and exert your will over, a large area.<br /> <br /> The thing is, people are struggling to give you much feedback because this is still a very half-baked concept for a character. It's a stat block with bits and pieces of a character tacked on, and not a lot of connective tissue explaining how it's all really supposed to fit together. This is why everyone keeps pushing you to think more about the character's specific motivations and values, because that would help us understand what the complete picture could possibly look like. If you're just looking for feedback on how the stat block would work as a recurring antagonist, then I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>'s advice from earlier is probably the best help you can realistically get under the circumstances: give her good defensive abilities and escape-buttons, and maybe be careful not to go overboard on her offensive abilities to make it less likely she's going to make a habit of murdering PCs when she shows up over and over.<br /> <br /> And beyond that, there just isn't much else people can say until you're ready to dig deeper into her actual identity as a character. And to the extent that you seem to have &quot;Metamorphosist&quot; as the core of her identity and motivations, the next logical step is to want to know more about the particular details of her research. It doesn't even need to be the focus of her entire unlife, but there is presumably a particular aspect of the vampire condition that she is currently focused on studying. Achieving the perfection of the vampire condition involves maximizing its strengths and removing its weaknesses, so those are the natural places to start. Is she studying the need for vitae to sustain unlife? Is she studying the vulnerability to the sun, or the effects of being staked? Conversely, is she studying the limits of the Disciplines, or the effects of the blood bond? All of these possibilities could lead to different preferences in test subjects for vivisection, for different kinds of experiments.<br /> <br /> Based on what you've mentioned up to now, it seems like a lot of focus is on the perfection of her physical form, seeing as how you have her focused on studying medicine and increasing her size and physical strength. But then you have her as a Koldun, who has also dabbled in Necromancy (I'm up to three possible uses in Metamorphosist research now). Unless you're tying this all together with some kind of theory of Metamorphosis that explains it all, it paints the picture of someone who doesn't really know *what* she's trying to achieve, just throwing everything at the wall to see what sticks. But really, it's seems like it's just a symptom of her stat block being a grab-bag of 'Rule of Cool' and Tzimisce stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Describing a Metamorphosist as focused on &quot;physical and spiritual transcendence,&quot; without any elaboration on what that means or how they are pursuing it, is a bit like asking a physicist what the subject of their research is and having them respond with &quot;physics.&quot; Sure, that's technically true, but it's ignoring the really interesting details. Is it particle physics, astrophysics, string theory?<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of interesting possibilities in what you've laid out so far, but she's not really going to be interesting until you develop her identity as a character instead of thinking about her as an obstacle for the PCs to overcome. Giving her a complex personality and fascinating motivations will make her a better antagonist than any stat block you can devise. My advice is to spend more time thinking about her choice to subsume her former packmates, because there's some interesting potential there, in terms of her general motivations and desires, but it could also be an angle to consider when it comes to her pursuit of Metamorphosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:15:38-07:00","id":1553117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553113#post1553113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I don't have a coterie I'm just putting out a concept for an NPC and want an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need a coterie and the basic idea is good, that's not the point.<br /> <br /> The thing is, with the exception of specific considerations for the particular PCs (or if there'll be PCs at all), none of the other questions require you to have an ongoing chronicle, or even a chronicle at all.<br /> <br /> Going back to the beginning of the thread: we can't evaluate the character stats without context. This context, though, may come from anything. You may be planning a city, you may be planning a novel, you may be telling stories in your head, you may be making a waifu for yourself, I've made all of those things myself, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> What matter is just that we need to know in broad strokes the story you're telling with her, where and how she lives and what she does, to have any meaningful opinion <i><b>on the stat block</b></i>. Not on the concept, the overall concept is cool.<br /> <br /> It's just that without knowing, for example, her approach to Azhi Dahaka in more detail, we can't say if anything in particular makes sense or not for her, or if a particular trait is explained by other aspect of her life, or if something calls for an alteration in her stats either up or down.<br /> <br /> Overall that's the problem with stat blocks for NPCs. With starting PCs we can, at least, say if their stats fulfill a given concept within their limited resources. NPCs, since they don't have limited resources, their context become even more important to say anything meaningful about the stat block.<br /> <br /> As far as addressing her without a story goes, I already did that in my first two posts: give her Strength 6 or 7, do the same with Perception and three or four Abilities, one Discipline at 7, for the rest you could distribute something like 5, 4, 4, 4, 3, 3, 3, 3, 2, 1. With Backgrounds, go wild. That would be a more organic starting point, although any particular decision would still go back to the need of context, a story to tell with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:38:06-07:00","id":1553119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553114#post1553114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're tying this all together with some kind of theory of Metamorphosis that explains it all, it paints the picture of someone who doesn't really know *what* she's trying to achieve, just throwing everything at the wall to see what sticks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't by itself a bad concept, either, nor makes her a weak character. It's just a concept that don't mesh well with lots of dots on those disparate Disciplines, because to have lots of dots in a Discipline takes commitment, and someone with this mindset isn't going to commit so much to something they're not so sure about.<br /> <br /> And the idea of her being a serial diablerist does work if the goal itself is to have lots of Discipline dots just 'cause, but then it would be interesting to know how she became so good at it and what that implies to her life and overall situation. Is she persecuted? Is she having trouble even within the Sabbat, or does she have enough clout to get away with <i>recurring</i> murder? Or does she focus on killing Camarilla vampires? Just keep in mind that even with Diablerie, this kind of mystical benefit usually means taking down powerful targets, preferably just as powerful or more than herself, otherwise the only benefits are blood and satisfying her addiction. By the way, is she addict to diablerie? If not, how did she avoid that? Diablerie may even <b>be</b> her research project to achieve Azhi Dahaka, she just need a theory behind it, a reason to think it will work.<br /> <br /> No answer is right or wrong, as long as there's a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:50:27-07:00","id":1553120,"title":"","content":"Well, the reason she fused with her lovers was done as a twisted form of affection or a display of dominance, she keeps them &quot;alive&quot; as a part of her by keeping their hearts inside her and connected to her system. She seeks to test the limits of the Vampiric condition both physically and spiritually with Animalism, Vicissitude, Protean and Necromancy, another reason I used all of those Disciplines is because there are some impressive combination disciplines that could be done with them. The revenant she fused with is still &quot;alive&quot; as a sort of zombie head that's attached to her chest. She has a habit of changing her skin color on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-12-2025, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T18:04:18-07:00","id":1553122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553119#post1553119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which isn't by itself a bad concept, either, nor makes her a weak character. It's just a concept that don't mesh well with lots of dots on those disparate Disciplines, because to have lots of dots in a Discipline takes commitment, and someone with this mindset isn't going to commit so much to something they're not so sure about.<br /> <br /> And the idea of her being a serial diablerist does work if the goal itself is to have lots of Discipline dots just 'cause, but then it would be interesting to know how she became so good at it and what that implies to her life and overall situation. Is she persecuted? Is she having trouble even within the Sabbat, or does she have enough clout to get away with <i>recurring</i> murder? Or does she focus on killing Camarilla vampires? Just keep in mind that even with Diablerie, this kind of mystical benefit usually means taking down powerful targets, preferably just as powerful or more than herself, otherwise the only benefits are blood and satisfying her addiction. By the way, is she addict to diablerie? If not, how did she avoid that? Diablerie may even <b>be</b> her research project to achieve Azhi Dahaka, she just need a theory behind it, a reason to think it will work.<br /> <br /> No answer is right or wrong, as long as there's a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed!<br /> <br /> The idea of diablerie as part of her Metamorphosis was also an angle I was considering, particularly in relation to my point regarding the potential connection with her decision to subsume her packmates. I was being coy before, but my thought there is that she might be pursuing an assimilation agenda, trying to become a greater being by incorporating others into herself. Her initial decision to merge with her peers might have been motivated by love, but it could have served as the inspiration for her interest in diablerie as a means to achieving perfection.<br /> <br /> I did have another thing I wanted to address, along the lines of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> saying &quot;no answer is right or wrong, as long as there's a story.&quot; When asked about the Discipline choices earlier, you mentioned how they were either chosen to support her Metamorphosist journey or as a means of remaining hidden. But there's one particular thing that doesn't (necessarily) seem to fit either of those categories: Presence. It doesn't seem like an obvious choice as a component of Metamorphosis, though I don't think it's impossible to make that case. It *definitely* doesn't fit with goal of remaining hidden, as Presence is all about being attention-grabbing. From a pragmatic perspective, Dominate would be better suited to the latter task, particularly if you reach the point of being able to alter memories. But to the extent that it does not (necessarily) fit either of those initial purposes, it has the potential to be viewed as an expression of a personal preference or desire that falls outside of her Metamorphosist goals, a possibility that could be interesting to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T18:17:45-07:00","id":1553123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553120#post1553120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the reason she fused with her lovers was done as a twisted form of affection or a display of dominance, she keeps them &quot;alive&quot; as a part of her by keeping their hearts inside her and connected to her system. She seeks to test the limits of the Vampiric condition both physically and spiritually with Animalism, Vicissitude, Protean and Necromancy, another reason I used all of those Disciplines is because there are some impressive combination disciplines that could be done with them. The revenant she fused with is still &quot;alive&quot; as a sort of zombie head that's attached to her chest. She has a habit of changing her skin color on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Double-posting because this reply came in as I was posting again, and the forum is very sensitive about editing posts immediately after they are made &gt;_&gt;)<br /> <br /> This starts to potentially stray into some messy territory. If the beings that she was fused with her were indisputably dead, then it'd be relatively straightforward. But the feat that you're talking about might be one of the most impressive feats of Vicissitude in the history of the Tzimisce Clan. I'd have to look more at the limits of Elder-level Vicissitude, but it may actually be impossible for her with &quot;only&quot; seven dots. It seems to be a more impressive accomplishment than that of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Velya_the_Vivisectionist_and_Elaine_Cassidy\" target=\"_blank\">Velya the Vivisectionist</a>. It's also worth noting that the act is slowly driving him mad and causing him to fall from the Path of Metamorphosis (though the fact that he merged himself with an actual Wight is definitely a contributing factor). Depending on how &quot;undead&quot; the vampires inside of her are, they could definitely be causing her a lot of psychological trauma if they aren't on board with their condition. Importantly, is having multiple vampiric hearts in her body meant to be an advantage or a liability (is staking one heart enough to paralyze her, or do you need to stake all three)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T18:30:40-07:00","id":1553124,"title":"","content":"That's why I started to think maybe she should be a Methuselah. Like I've said before the reason she's so tall is because she merged her body with her lovers, she used to be 6 feet tall until she merged with them, now only their heads and hearts remain intact as a part of her. They are a bit upset at being merged with her. You have to stake her heart specifically to stun her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T09:12:27-07:00","id":1553139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553124#post1553124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I started to think maybe she should be a Methuselah. Like I've said before the reason she's so tall is because she merged her body with her lovers, she used to be 6 feet tall until she merged with them, now only their heads and hearts remain intact as a part of her. They are a bit upset at being merged with her. You have to stake her heart specifically to stun her.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be a bad idea, but you would be moving her beyond the level of antagonist for a typical coterie; even a 6th Generation vampire is a pretty overwhelming threat if its had time to fully develop its potential. But if you just want to push the character concept to its fullest, she would probably be a paragon of the Path of Metamorphosis, with Vicissitude 8. Maybe a childe of Yorak from the early Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> If they aren't willingly part of her, then you might want to look at giving her some Derangements to reflect their influence on her psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T09:49:05-07:00","id":1553140,"title":"","content":"well, there's a combination discipline called Komnenos' Honor which helps with staying on a path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T13:32:21-07:00","id":1553145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553140#post1553140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, there's a combination discipline called Komnenos' Honor which helps with staying on a path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a high Path rating wouldn't necessarily stop her from having Derangements caused by the presence of two unliving souls trapped in her body.<br /> <br /> Also, Combination Disciplines are often unique tricks that a particular vampire has come up with for their personal use. It's not realistic to have one character packing a grocery list of them, on top of unique Elder-level Disciplines. So for an NPC that you actually intend to use, be careful not to go overboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T14:32:01-07:00","id":1553146,"title":"","content":"Ah, so you're saying that combination Disciplines can only be used by one person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T15:01:49-07:00","id":1553147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553146#post1553146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so you're saying that combination Disciplines can only be used by one person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Think of them like secret techniques. After someone invents one, only the people they choose to teach will know them. Since they're like secret weapons, people don't share them lightly. And the fact that you need ranks in multiple Disciplines means that less people have the skills to learn them and pass them along.<br /> <br /> They're just much rarer than the regular Disciplines, so having one person with a whole bunch of them is extremely unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T20:54:03-07:00","id":1553157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553123#post1553123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This starts to potentially stray into some messy territory. If the beings that she was fused with her were indisputably dead, then it'd be relatively straightforward. But the feat that you're talking about might be one of the most impressive feats of Vicissitude in the history of the Tzimisce Clan. I'd have to look more at the limits of Elder-level Vicissitude, but it may actually be impossible for her with &quot;only&quot; seven dots. It seems to be a more impressive accomplishment than that of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Velya_the_Vivisectionist_and_Elaine_Cassidy\" target=\"_blank\">Velya the Vivisectionist</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't think it's that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> Velya, to begin with, &quot;only&quot; has <b>Vicissitude 7</b>, so entirely within reach of a 6th Gen. And the effect doesn't seem more impressive, it seems to be pretty much the same.<br /> <br /> Also of note, Velya's write-up doesn't exactly imply this feat to be excepcional in execution, and even the consequences are more tied to the fact that Cassidy was already a <i>Wight</i> when they conjoined (not to mention that she was a poor choice overall, she was an &quot;evil&quot;, overly destructive child, her descent into wightdom was a given, really).<br /> <br /> Unless the conjoining gives any benefit at all that can't be surmised by other traits (like giving greater Strength, but &quot;actually&quot; bought like normal), there's no reason to think this can be done with a <b>Vicissitude 6</b> power, or even just with normal levels of <b>Vicissitude</b>, if coupled with a lot of Medicine and Fleshcraft rolls. Mechanically the most that can happen is that the subsumed characters may still have their own actions (although probably a very limited range of actions), but still acting on their own.<br /> <br /> Overall the idea with Velya isn't that conjoining was a challenge, but just that it was overall a bad idea. This is totally doable here, with less impact (but still some impact) since no <i>Wights</i> are involved. <i>Yet</i>. Of course, she also has to feed them individually, even if they're limited only to the Blood needed to awake each night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553140#post1553140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, there's a combination discipline called Komnenos' Honor which helps with staying on a path.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't strictly necessary if you can explain her Path Rating in other ways. We have to first determine how the other minds affect her, how this may affect her Path (or not), and what other strategies she may have to deal with the problem and still advance in her Path. We also have to determine her Path Rating, as the lowest it is, the easier it is to maintain. Just because she's reaching for apotheosis doesn't means she's currently being as successful as she would like or even believe. In the end, Paths are hard, and they're supposed to be. Most vampires aren't very high even when they're dedicated.<br /> <br /> As an NPC you only should give her a power like <b><i>Komnenos' Honor</i></b> if you plan on having her regularly act <i>against</i> her Path in a story. This is not about explaining her, this is about characterizing her. A power has to ultimately be there to be used. <b><i>Komnenos' Honor</i></b>\u200bimplies a character that sins and stills don't fall, not a character that doesn't sin.<br /> <br /> Its also important to think what are the consequences of her having her lovers subsumed alive. While it doesn't have to be a low Path Rating, or a hard time staying on the Path, there has to be something. <i>Derangements</i> are a good option as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Kharnov</a> suggested, although there may be other options. It doesn't necessarily have to affect her stats directly, but you should give it serious consideration.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553146#post1553146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so you're saying that combination Disciplines can only be used by one person?</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice, both Elder Level Disciplines and Combo Disciplines are usually developed by the character by themselves, with no help, a lot of effort and no instinct guiding it, so most characters have a relatively low number of them. But this isn't a hard rule. A vampire that has one can teach another that fulfills the requisites, and that's a lot easier (if not cheaper in XP), but's also a lot rare precisely because they're too valuable. Parallel development also exists, so two unconnected characters may happen to have the same power, but that should be exceedingly rare.<br /> <br /> While for game effects the lists of such powers help building characters and giving players and STs options to work with, in-game nothing guarantees that any of them is available, or even exists at all at the moment.<br /> <br /> A lot of it is up to the ST, though, and while the frequency of a <i>particular</i> power should always be low, the frequency of <i>any</i> vampire having <i>some</i> Combo Disciplines is up in the air, as is even the age at which they usually appear. Because they're very rare in official stat blocks, it's usually accepted that they're very rare, to the point that even among Elders few have them. But this hasn't to be the case for your character.<br /> <br /> You should also keep in mind how attuned to the character they are. Don't choose Disciplines based on the Combos you want, you're free to made-up Combos and Elder Level powers that fit her specifically, based on whatever she in fact has that you think makes sense. This isn't a bad choice, it's actually how those powers are meant to be used.<br /> <br /> Going for my suggestion on Discipline distribution, one way to make it feel organic could be to give her one or two Combos, then trade Discipline dots for more combos if you want, a number of Combos equal to the level of the dot you gave up (so reducing a 5 dots Discipline to 4 dots would give you 5 powers). This isn't strictly how the XP for such powers work, but would give you a good ballpark on how much different powers she should have.<br /> <br /> Oh, and another thing: take care to not overdo it, in practice giving too many different powers to a character has a great chance of just making the character harder to use (for anything) than really making them more powerful or more effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T09:33:32-07:00","id":1553172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553157#post1553157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't think it's that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> Velya, to begin with, &quot;only&quot; has <b>Vicissitude 7</b>, so entirely within reach of a 6th Gen. And the effect doesn't seem more impressive, it seems to be pretty much the same.<br /> <br /> Also of note, Velya's write-up doesn't exactly imply this feat to be excepcional in execution, and even the consequences are more tied to the fact that Cassidy was already a <i>Wight</i> when they conjoined (not to mention that she was a poor choice overall, she was an &quot;evil&quot;, overly destructive child, her descent into wightdom was a given, really).<br /> <br /> Unless the conjoining gives any benefit at all that can't be surmised by other traits (like giving greater Strength, but &quot;actually&quot; bought like normal), there's no reason to think this can be done with a <b>Vicissitude 6</b> power, or even just with normal levels of <b>Vicissitude</b>, if coupled with a lot of Medicine and Fleshcraft rolls. Mechanically the most that can happen is that the subsumed characters may still have their own actions (although probably a very limited range of actions), but still acting on their own.<br /> <br /> Overall the idea with Velya isn't that conjoining was a challenge, but just that it was overall a bad idea. This is totally doable here, with less impact (but still some impact) since no <i>Wights</i> are involved. <i>Yet</i>. Of course, she also has to feed them individually, even if they're limited only to the Blood needed to awake each night.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a fair point. I haven't looked too closely into the details of how integrated Elaine is into Velya's body, so I'm kind of basing it on the assumption that she's just kind of stuck onto his back, like the image. Having their entire bodies subsumed, with only their hearts and heads and the circulatory system connecting them intact does seem to be a bit more advanced than that. But my whole understanding of the situation could be faulty.<br /> <br /> I realized that the Blood Brothers and their unique Discipline, Sanguinus, could be a useful source of ideas for such a thing, both IC and OOC. They manage to pull off something somewhat similar with just 5 dots, so it doesn't have to be a Methuselah-level achievement. But using higher levels of the Discipline could justify having less to worry about in terms of potential drawbacks.<br /> <br /> I'd actually considered making an argument that the NPCs decision to integrate her lovers into her body might be a sign of her disregarding the tenets of Metamorphosis, much like Velya. But looking closer, it's at least somewhat distinct. Velya did what he did out of concern for the needs of his childe (trying to save her from Wightdom), which runs afoul of the Path's opposition to caring about the needs of others. But to the extent that this NPC did it purely on the basis of their own desires means that it doesn't (necessarily) contradict the tenets of Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> I do wonder whether or not forcefully subsuming vampires like this might not drive them to madness or Wightdom even if they weren't like that before.<br /> <br /> Good points about the possibility for actions (even if they're only mental ones) for the subsumed vampires, as well as pointing out that they would require additional vitae to sustain them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T11:01:39-07:00","id":1553177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553172#post1553172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do wonder whether or not forcefully subsuming vampires like this might not drive them to madness or Wightdom even if they weren't like that before.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably isn't doing any good to their mental health, definitely. I just don't think it has to be necessarily handled in a particular way, so I'll give the author the freedom to think what to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T19:42:03-07:00","id":1553190,"title":"","content":"Well, a reason she'd use Komnenos' Honor is because she does occasionally indulge herself in pleasures such as blood wine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T21:03:54-07:00","id":1553195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553177#post1553177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably isn't doing any good to their mental health, definitely. I just don't think it has to be necessarily handled in a particular way, so I'll give the author the freedom to think what to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, giving her Derangements was just a suggestion, not necessarily the best or only way to handle it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553190#post1553190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a reason she'd use Komnenos' Honor is because she does occasionally indulge herself in pleasures such as blood wine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were you planning on her being at 9 or 10 dots on the Path? Indulging in pleasure isn't a sin before then, and grabbing a Combination Discipline just so she can enjoy a drink guilt-free seems kind of overkill. But I admittedly don't know anything about the history of Komnenos' Honor, so I can't speak to the likelihood of her encountering the opportunity to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-15T01:57:40-07:00","id":1553199,"title":"","content":"It seems okay, the two big changes id have are is id loose necromancy since she already has a form of blood magic, its quite a niche power and it doesn't really overlap with her interests outside of the Mortis path corpse within the monster.<br /> <br /> The second issue I can notice is she needs more backgrounds to reflect her footprint on the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-18T15:02:23-07:00","id":1553259,"title":"","content":"I raised the resources Background to 5. Maybe I could add contacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-18-2025, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-18T22:16:33-07:00","id":1553264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553259#post1553259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I raised the resources Background to 5. Maybe I could add contacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Backgrounds are the only place in the stats you shouldn't pull any punches. The only limit should be what's even relevant to state in the stats, and any value below 5 should be a calculated weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T08:17:10-07:00","id":1553266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553264#post1553264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds are the only place in the stats you shouldn't pull any punches. The only limit should be what's even relevant to state in the stats, and any value below 5 should be a calculated weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think having some Backgrounds at &quot;only&quot; 4 could be reasonable, representing areas she has committed a little less attention, without regarding it as a serious weakness or vulnerability. The amount of time she has spent on her skills and Disciplines would explain her having spent a little less time expanding her material and social resources.<br /> <br /> But beyond that, yeah, give her any and all Backgrounds that fit within the concept/story that you've thought up for her. In a previous post, you mentioned her having access to human trafficking networks. That means you should probably give her Herd, unless you have a specific reason she wouldn't keep vessels on hand.<br /> <br /> Unless she's part of some kind of attack force that just moved into a new territory, she should probably have Domain. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, Tzimisce, and Koldun in particular, are known for putting down roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T10:42:39-07:00","id":1553267,"title":"","content":"Okay, I gave her a few more in backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T14:36:42-07:00","id":1553305,"title":"","content":"So, if i'm getting things right, Evelyn is basically something like a self-aware <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vozhd\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vozhd</b></a> in the form of a giant muscle mommy, because as a self-aware being she finds the typical vozhd look icky.<br /> Or maybe more precisely, since she's very much a vampire and not a ghoul, the most successful <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sanguinus\" target=\"_blank\">Coagulated Entity</a> ever.<br /> <br /> Me, i would start from the requirements to create a Vozhd (Vissicitude 6, Blood Magic 3 in DA?) and use Animalism, Auspex &amp; Dominate 4-5 each to explain her subsuming all the allies/retainers/etc in one body without having to lobotomize them all as is usually done. So 7th generation could suffice and 6th cover bases well enough.<br /> <br /> Considering Vissicitude 5 already lets one shapechange from flesh to blood, Vissicitude 6 is justification enough for one to go &quot;gank mass, gank physics&quot; and her to be able to compress into a more average-sized form if into the mood for discretion or stealth, all of her &quot;children&quot; existing as &quot;memories&quot; within her veins until she calls them out as faces on her flesh, extra limbs, reforms them from drops of her vitae like gory summons and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> Drawing on the Vozhd and Coagulated Entity parallels, she could maybe be involved in some manner with the blood magic research within Sabbat ranks that led to the creation of modern methods of Vozhd crafting (where you can get them done by a group effort of non-elder tier vicissitude users) and/or the founding Blood Brothers bloodline, possibly having some status and prestige associated with these feats. Maybe some honorary title of &quot;Mother of Sanguinus&quot; among the bloodline? Sounds fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, i feel like one can do what the OP aims for and some more just fine with &quot;mere&quot; Vissicitude 6 and 7th gen, what is quite respectable without too being crazy and calling for lots of lore/worldbuiling gymnastics like a 5th or 4th gen.<br /> (Damn, vanilla 13-8th generation kindred might be quite acceptable too, if you like me toys with the homebrew idea of the Aura/Bearing of a high level Path letting a character develop stats beyond their generation limits, for example)<br /> <br /> <br /> The fact she has the Szantovich surname is very interesting too imho, since it kind of implies she's from a time before the family changed name to Zantosa (what i think happened sometime between the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Omen_War\" target=\"_blank\">Omen War</a> and the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anarch_Revolt#First_Anarch_Revolt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarch Revolt</a>/foundation of the Sabbat) and does not wholy share the Sabbat's mindset of contempt for human ties &amp; heritage, maybe pointing out to her being a dark ages koldunist that was actually in torpor during most, if not all, of the Revolt and only joined the sect centuries later? Just a thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope some of these ramblings of mine sound entertaining and are not too redundant with other posters' suggestions and thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2025, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T18:16:58-07:00","id":1553312,"title":"","content":"Well, you were right in that her surname implies her age. She fused with two other Cainites while claiming the arms and head of one of her revenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T23:07:06-07:00","id":1553317,"title":"","content":"Good to know. So does the surname she currently holds to comes from this particular revenant? <b><i>Very </i></b>interesting in the degree of emotional attachment to that retainer such a decision seems to imply. On one side it raises the question if &quot;Mr. Szantovich&quot; was not the oldest part in that &quot;cooperative of minds&quot;, a special ghoul inherited from an even older vampire that played the role of sire or mentor for Evelyn in in the past.<br /> <br /> On another, that kind of emotional connection to people, even if twisted by contemporary moral mores, seems to imply with an attitude toward people more in synch with the Tzimisce from before the Anarch Revolt, or at least before the crystalization of the Sabbat's view on kindred superiority to Humanity and rejection of mortal values &amp; connection.<br /> <br /> So, even if indeed younger than her subsumed servant-lover, she might be decently old - like a kindred from the 1400s with a lover of the 1200s among her retainers, for an example.<br /> Or someone whose early references in the formation of an identity as kindred were mentors or retainers of such age, at least.<br /> <br /> Because, on a little aside, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evelyn_(name)\" target=\"_blank\">names</a> have meaning and a history of sorts of their own to boot. And can tell us all kind of things, about a person's origins or the enviroment her forefathers were part of.<br /> <br /> <br /> But those two other Cainites she fused with, what can you tell us about them?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T08:16:44-07:00","id":1553323,"title":"","content":"Well, her name is Szantovich because she was born as a Revenant before getting embraced. While her two lovers that she assimilated were actually two of her pack mates. One was a Nosferatu and the other was a Gangrel. The Revenant she absorbed was actually a fairly recent addition to her body, a woman named Adriana Zantosa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T18:41:04-07:00","id":1553358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553323#post1553323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, her name is Szantovich because she was born as a Revenant before getting embraced. While her two lovers that she assimilated were actually two of her pack mates. One was a Nosferatu and the other was a Gangrel. The Revenant she absorbed was actually a fairly recent addition to her body, a woman named Adriana Zantosa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so she's indeed from the time the family still called itself Szantovich. Guess i misinterpreted you previous post.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on when was she embraced or if she ever spent some time in torpor? Her being more &quot;old country&quot; and somewhat (imho at least) out of synch with contemporary Sabbat mores gives me &quot;medieval/renaissance Tzimisce that went to sleep and only returned in the last century or half-century&quot; vibes so to speak.<br /> Someone mostly in the fringes of the sect where no one will bother and vice-versa, until something catches her interest (like the Vozhds &amp; Blood Brothers experiments, i guess) and she pulls off the kind of stunts that <i>then </i>everybody notices.<br /> <br /> Also, how much in agreement or not were her two packmates with the merge itself? Do they still manifest themselves and to what degree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-21-2025, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T18:47:13-07:00","id":1553391,"title":"","content":"Well, as I've said before, she merged with her two lovers against their will. She used to be six feet tall and her new height of 16 feet is from the accumulated mass of her two lovers. Their heads are still on her right below the breasts while she has their hearts in her chest cavity along with her own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T07:22:26-07:00","id":1553511,"title":"","content":"I finally decided on what dots to use in Disciplines so I edited the post. Also, in terms of combination disciplines She has Ears of the Bat, Wound Sculpting and Komnenos' Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-28-2025, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T08:43:33-07:00","id":1553514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553511#post1553511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally decided on what dots to use in Disciplines so I edited the post. Also, in terms of combination disciplines She has Ears of the Bat, Wound Sculpting and Komnenos' Honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>She can't have Vicissitude 10, &quot;just&quot; 9.<br /> <br /> Ten is for the 3rd Generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T11:29:11-07:00","id":1553517,"title":"","content":"Really? Are you sure? Cause I remember that what was restricted to Antediluvians was the Plot Device power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 08-28-2025, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T14:37:54-07:00","id":1553526,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> explained before, each Generation below 8th adds one extra &quot;dot&quot; that you can have in Traits, Disciplines, etc.<br /> <br /> So 7th Generation can have 6 dots.<br /> 6th Generation can have 7 dots.<br /> 5th Generation can have 8 dots.<br /> And 4th Generation can have 9 dots.<br /> <br /> 10 dots is limited to Vampires of the Third Generation (or lower).<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. After taking a closer look at the sheet again, a couple of comments.<br /> <br /> First, the Kraina and the Ways of &quot;modern&quot; Koldunic Sorcery are generally considered incompatible (though it's been a while and I can't remember if there's an official ruling on it, tbh; I'lltry to find it when I get home later). The lore behind it is that the Kraina came from the traditional practices of Koldunism, while the Ways were a product of the Tzimisce making pacts with Kupala for greater power. So you should probably decide whether you want her using the Kraina or the Ways; she's old enough to reasonably have either option available, though I think the Kraina are mostly used by the Old Clan in the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> Secondly, for a 4th Generation vampire from the Dark Ages, her Attributes and Abilities are probably a bit too low, with nothing over 5 that I could see. Given how many different skills and Disciplines she has, she doesn't necessarily need a bunch of 6+ traits, or many at the maximum limit allowed by her Generation, but she should probably be 'superhuman' in some areas, like Strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Comments on updated stats 08-28-2025, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T16:36:09-07:00","id":1553528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553526#post1553526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> explained before, each Generation below 8th adds one extra &quot;dot&quot; that you can have in Traits, Disciplines, etc.<br /> <br /> So 7th Generation can have 6 dots.<br /> 6th Generation can have 7 dots.<br /> 5th Generation can have 8 dots.<br /> And 4th Generation can have 9 dots.<br /> <br /> 10 dots is limited to Vampires of the Third Generation (or lower).<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. After taking a closer look at the sheet again, a couple of comments.<br /> <br /> First, the Kraina and the Ways of &quot;modern&quot; Koldunic Sorcery are generally considered incompatible (though it's been a while and I can't remember if there's an official ruling on it, tbh; I'lltry to find it when I get home later). The lore behind it is that the Kraina came from the traditional practices of Koldunism, while the Ways were a product of the Tzimisce making pacts with Kupala for greater power. So you should probably decide whether you want her using the Kraina or the Ways; she's old enough to reasonably have either option available, though I think the Kraina are mostly used by the Old Clan in the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> Secondly, for a 4th Generation vampire from the Dark Ages, her Attributes and Abilities are probably a bit too low, with nothing over 5 that I could see. Given how many different skills and Disciplines she has, she doesn't necessarily need a bunch of 6+ traits, or many at the maximum limit allowed by her Generation, but she should probably be 'superhuman' in some areas, like Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>But bloodlines have their own disciplines that go up to ten even though they don't have Antediluvians, only Methuselahs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T17:59:21-07:00","id":1553529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553528#post1553528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But bloodlines have their own disciplines that go up to ten even though they don't have Antediluvians, only Methuselahs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Bloodline-specific Discipline I can recall going up to 10 dots is Daimonion, and that's complicated by various aspects of Baali lore making it possible for there to potentially be a Third or Second Generation member of their Bloodline.<br /> <br /> Also, vampires that achieve Golconda can possibly (Storyteller's discretion) unlock the ability to learn Traits and Disciplines beyond their Generation limit. There are a few other ways around it. But the normal limit is the one I mentioned above. If you want to try to find a way around it, that is your prerogative, but you would be talking about one of the most special snowflakes to ever exist in the lore of VtM at that point.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T23:16:43-07:00","id":1553531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553528#post1553528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But bloodlines have their own disciplines that go up to ten even though they don't have Antediluvians, only Methuselahs.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most cases they're not canonically expected to exist at such levels, some aren't even expected to get near it (not all Bloodlines have Methuselah, not all of them even have members of lower Generation than 8th, it varies a lot), but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> said there are a few ways around it.<br /> <br /> Mostly they're there because lowering Generation is a thing. Even getting to 3rd Generation doesn't require anything not already in the rules and the setting, so in some chronicle somewhere it will happen. So this is reason #1, you can always have a character (PC or NPC) that somehow got there, even if it's only in a given chronicle, and still be &quot;legal&quot;.<br /> <br /> The #2 reason is that no character is limited to only maxing out their In-Clans. So while there's no <b>Daughter of Cacophony</b> below 6th Generation (if that much) even in legend, any 3rd Generation, including pretty active people like Tremere, Saulot and Augustus Giovanni, may develop higher levels of <b><i>Melpominee</i></b>, they just have to learn it first.<br /> <br /> And #3 common way to achieve 10th level Disciplines, that I already mentioned before, is Golconda. One relatively common effect of Golconda is the limit on Disciplines (and on Disciplines only) being removed. <b>Those</b> characters can achieve 10 dots in any Discipline, just like an Ante, as long as they have the XP to do so. This has never been actually applied to many NPCs at all, even NPCs that did achieve Golconda, and none has 10 dots, but is still legal by the rules. There's some history and nuance to this ruling, but overall that's the gist of it.<br /> <br /> But none of those ways to achieve a Discipline at 10 is anything nearly reliable or expected. Being 3rd Generation is way, way more contrived than being &quot;just&quot; a Methuselah. Golconda shouldn't be possible to reach through a Path of Enlightenment, it's specifically a Humanity thing.<br /> <br /> Overall, anyway, level 10 Discipline is overkill. Level 9 powers can already be godlike feats. By the way, the &quot;Plot Device&quot; isn't an effect restricted to Antes, it's a simplification of the rules for level 10 as specifying powers at this level is mostly useless. This was done once in a very old supplement, but by <i>Gehenna</i> the book the devs decided that making rules for powers at this level is a waste of time. So, yeah, a non-Ante has basically a limited number of powers, but those are just barely defined Plot Devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T00:59:00-07:00","id":1553533,"title":"","content":"(The forum ate my post while editing....)<br /> <br /> There IS a loophole in your case for Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <br /> Make her an <b>Asakku</b>, a Kindred whose souls have been corrupted by excessive use of Vicissitude (see The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra)<br /> As a vampire on the Path of the Asakku - a Path on its own right, but less an ideology than a state of being prompted by the obsessive study of Vicissitude and communion with the dark intelligences behind it* - increasingly surrenders to her Vicissitude she gains special abilities. These Transmutations represent the Discipline's will expanding into other Cainites and living things, and its ability to take firmer hold of the vampire's consciousness.<br /> <br /> As a vampire on the Path of the Asakku increasingly surrenders to her Vicissitude she gains special abilities. These Transmutations represent the Discipline's will expanding into other Cainites and living things, and its ability to take firmer hold of the vampire's consciousness. A follower of the Path gains <i>Sinister Mastery</i> at the first dot of the Path, and another Transmutation of the player's choice at every even numbered dot thereafter.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Transmutations</b></u><br /> <b>Sinister Mastery</b> - This ability (possessed by all Asakku) reduces the Vicissitude experience cost multiplier by 1. Combination Disciplines featuring Vicissitude are purchased at half cost, rounded up.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Infection</b> - The Asakku drains a vampire of all of her blood and fills half of her blood pool with the Asakku's own. The Vampire becomes an Asakku and is converted to the Path of Asakku at a one dot rating, and trades one dot of her weakest Discipline for a dot of Vicissitude if she doesn't have any dots. One she reaches four dots in Vicissitude she can advance further up the Path of Asakku. Blood Infection counts as two steps towards the blood bond.<br /> <br /> <b>Inner Babble</b> - The Asakku's mind is filled with sounds and images, and her Aura shows random emotions. Telepathy attempts and attempts to read the Asakku's aura fail.<br /> <br /> <b>Occultation</b> - The Asakku's increasingly alien nature becomes something the very Earth seeks to abjure. Fate erases the Corrupted's footsteps. Freak events erase records of her presence. This Transmutation may be selected multiple times.Potentiation - The Asakku Vicissitude rating can exceed her Generational maximum by one dot. The power can be taken up to three times, but cannot exceed nine dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeding the Garden</b> - The Asakku infects the soil of an area with their vitae. Any animal who eats the plants or drinks water from this area becomes the Asakku's ghoul after a month. If the animal is eaten, the predator becomes the Asakku's ghoul.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Whispers</b> - Any creatures who have drunk the blood, had Vicissitude used on them by the Asakku, or had the Sinister Obsession derangement can have the Asakku use their senses, use the Auspex, Animalism, Dominate, and Vicissitude Disciplines through this connection as if they were touching them, and relay emotions and instincts, such as the sense that someone the target sees is an enemy (though not information explaining why this is so). If the target possesses at least a dot in Vicissitude, the Corrupted may utilize any rank of Vicissitude through the target, using it as a proxy.<br /> <br /> And what you &quot;need&quot; in this case:<br /> <br /> <b>Potentiation</b> - The Asakku Vicissitude rating can exceed her Generational maximum by one dot. The power can be taken up to three times, but cannot exceed nine dots.<br /> <br /> Still you would not have Vicissitude 10, but can climb up to 9 without making your Elder one of the direct Child of an Antediluvian<br /> <br /> As a Tzimisce there is another quasi-cannonical way to do it; metamorphosists of Clan Tzimisce <i>theoretically</i> could push beyond 9 dots through their <b>quest to transcend vampirism</b><br /> Because, well, they want to transcend Vampirsim... and it limit (Clanbook Tzimsice Revised)<br /> <br /> <br /> A curious relative of Vicissitude, <b>Sanguinus</b>, the Discipline of the Blood Brothers have a power, <i>Walk of Caine</i> that temporarily lower your generation by raising that of others in your circle, BUT no matter how big the circle, no Blood Brother can drop to an effective Generation lower than Fourth. Likewise, a Thirteenth Generation Blood Brother can drop to an effective Generation of Fourteenth, (Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition/ Guide to the Sabbat )<br /> But again, there is no actual rule against other Kindred to learn Sanguinus under specific circumstances, but need some work, to actually use it, like having a circle; usually diablerizing a Blood Brother works. For a single vampire to use its full powers, they must be in a blood-bound circle with at least one other vampire with Sanguinus knowledge.<br /> So if you REALLY want to take this, <i>theoretically</i>\u200b her child/team and her\u200b could eat the Blood Brother cicrcle <i>thecnically </i>replacing them - then keep them in VERY tigh blood bond and in the basement.<br /> <br /> With<b> Demonic Investments </b>(see Players Guide to the Sabbat\u200b , Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat, Infernalism: The Path of Screams and The Book of Madness) <i>theoretically</i>\u200b you can make a Pact to use Disciplines beyond your Generation cap it is framed as \u201cbypassing normal limits\u201d rather than true Generational change<br /> But hey, if you sell your soul already, you can go all the way, why not?<br /> Your Game<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally... <b>From Marduk's Throat </b>(Sins of the Blood, Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, and Lore of the Clans) a <b>Dur-An-Ki </b>or <b>Assamite Sorcery </b>Ritual\u200b<br /> Each ritual takes eight hours to produce one fourth of a blood point To decrease their generation, an Assamite must consume a number of points of this alchemical blood equal to the maximum blood point value of a vampire of the desired generation. The subject of the ritual need not to be the Vizier who prepared the concoction, but all of the blood used for this generation decrease must be made by the same Vizier in the same laboratory. No more than one week may pass between one use of this ritual and the next for a single drop in generation, or all of the existing elixir will spoil and be rendered useless.\u200b<br /> The \u200bLore of the Clan version is a bith harsher, to reduce the drinker\u2019s Generation by one level, the potion must incorporate a number of blood points from vampires of lower Generation than the drinker equal to four times the maximum blood point value of the desired Generation.<br /> The original version of the ritual did not allow access to some of the lower Generations because of the preparation time compared to the conservation time of each Ritual, since a quarter point of blood was equivalent to 8h of ritual and the result of this ritual could not last more than a week. (Example: To reach the 4th Generation it would have taken 50 (Blood Pool) multiplied by 4 then multiplied again by 8, which give us a nice 1600h to make the full Ritual. That's more than 9 weeks... unless you can work around that <i>somehow</i><br /> <br /> Anyhow, there are not many ways to do that level 10 Discipline, but again, while powers are nice and all, why would you need a level 10 Vicissitude anyway? The only canonical power is Reform Body, to recreate your body after dying<br /> Cheaper to just take <b>Nine Lives </b>Merit (Fate has granted you the opportunity to come as close to Final Death as anyone can get and still survive. When a rolls occurs that would results in your death, the roll is made again. If the next roll succeeds, then you live and one of your nine lives is used up)<br /> And &quot;<b>Plot Device</b>&quot; - aka. whatever the plot needs. Okay... just... lets face it, as a Storyteller you already have this &quot;power&quot;...<br /> <br /> But again, you don't need a 4h generation eldrich abomination to make your players unlife a living hell with powers...<br /> I mean if you want to scare the unliving shit of them just throw a Baal at hem with <b>Unleash Hell's Fury/Adramelech's Wrath</b>\u200b to cause a Cainite to feel the Sun's light no matter what shelter they have\u200b and burn them as if the Sun itself were shining upon them. Not kill them just to feel how totally helpless they are against even a 5th generation Matuselah (they are a bit more common them a 4th)<br /> There are even &quot;weaker&quot; powers to twist them in to submission and realize how dangerous your Elder, you don't really need shiny high-octane powers... just sayin'<br /> <br /> Of course as others pointed out, your game, your story<br /> But in my humble opinion you over complicate this whole thing\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T01:08:15-07:00","id":1553534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There IS a loophole in your case for Vicissitude</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this' the best way of phrasing it, as your points are ways to have <b>Vicissitude 9</b> with a higher Generation, not a way to have <b>Vicissitude 10</b>, which is what they want.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there are ways to achieve up to 9 dots without being 4th Gen, ways that aren't much more contrived than being 4th Gen in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But again, you don't need a 4h generation eldrich abomination to make your players unlife a living hell with powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point. Page 3, post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/43\" >Wraith: The Oblivion 20th Anniversary Edition</a> The character <u><b>is</b></u> the point.<br /> <br /> So there's no use in exploring alternative characters, we're working a specific character concept into a stat block.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T08:36:24-07:00","id":1553538,"title":"","content":"The reason I want them to have 10 is for Reform Body. It would make them unpredictable and hard to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T10:51:29-07:00","id":1553539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553538#post1553538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I want them to have 10 is for Reform Body. It would make them unpredictable and hard to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reform Body doesn't make a vampire &quot;hard to kill.&quot; It makes them virtually indestructible. Though they added some conditions later (it needs to reform through the flesh and blood of its progeny), this is one of the signature powers of the Tzimisce Antediluvian, which allowed it to come back after being destroyed in his duel with Samiel, founder of the Warrior Caste Salubri.<br /> <br /> Wanting to give this power to a character means wanting to give that character the power of an Antediluvian. You're not talking about an NPC anymore, you're talking about a walking Deus Ex Machina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T10:57:11-07:00","id":1553540,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so you're saying that they reform through their own Childer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T11:19:10-07:00","id":1553542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553540#post1553540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, so you're saying that they reform through their own Childer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to begin with. It's a plot device for The Elder to effectively be a disease within the entire clan.<br /> <br /> Making her hard to kill is plenty doable below 10.<br /> <br /> Suggestion: make for her a Combo Discipline with Vicissitude and Auspex that let her survive in Astral form, possess people and then turn the new body into her old one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T11:27:29-07:00","id":1553544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553542#post1553542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, to begin with. It's a plot device for The Elder to effectively be a disease within the entire clan.<br /> <br /> Making her hard to kill is plenty doable below 10.<br /> <br /> Suggestion: make for her a Combo Discipline with Vicissitude and Auspex that let her survive in Astral form, possess people and then turn the new body into her old one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool idea. I was considering something similar: a power that lets her 'give birth' to her own reincarnation in the form of a vampiric corpse-baby, maybe as a Combo Discipline with Koldunic Sorcery. Potentially with the limit of having to temporarily raise her Generation by one for each reincarnation she creates. It has the benefit of placing a limit on how many 'respawns' she can have waiting in the wings, with the ability for an informed enemy to try and track them down and destroy them before seeking to finish her off, like a phylactery. If the main body dies, the reincarnation awakens and quickly regrows to her full strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T21:12:53-07:00","id":1553561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553533#post1553533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally... <b>From Marduk's Throat </b>(Sins of the Blood, Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, and Lore of the Clans) a <b>Dur-An-Ki </b>or <b>Assamite Sorcery </b>Ritual<br /> Each ritual takes eight hours to produce one fourth of a blood point To decrease their generation, an Assamite must consume a number of points of this alchemical blood equal to the maximum blood point value of a vampire of the desired generation. The subject of the ritual need not to be the Vizier who prepared the concoction, but all of the blood used for this generation decrease must be made by the same Vizier in the same laboratory. No more than one week may pass between one use of this ritual and the next for a single drop in generation, or all of the existing elixir will spoil and be rendered useless.\u200b<br /> The \u200bLore of the Clan version is a bith harsher, to reduce the drinker\u2019s Generation by one level, the potion must incorporate a number of blood points from vampires of lower Generation than the drinker equal to four times the maximum blood point value of the desired Generation.<br /> The original version of the ritual did not allow access to some of the lower Generations because of the preparation time compared to the conservation time of each Ritual, since a quarter point of blood was equivalent to 8h of ritual and the result of this ritual could not last more than a week. (Example: To reach the 4th Generation it would have taken 50 (Blood Pool) multiplied by 4 then multiplied again by 8, which give us a nice 1600h to make the full Ritual. That's more than 9 weeks... unless you can work around that <i>somehow</i>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intent on the week-long limit was &quot;you had to do the ritual at least once a week to keep the elixir fresh&quot; and not &quot;you only have a single week to produce all of the blood you need,&quot; otherwise that gets pretty useless pretty fast, even ignoring all the other material costs and making sure your Sorcerer doesn't die/fall into torpor/botch/get distracted and forget to work on it/etc.<br /> <br /> It <i>has </i>been ages since I cracked those books open, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T19:10:16-07:00","id":1554885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1553122#post1553122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed!<br /> <br /> The idea of diablerie as part of her Metamorphosis was also an angle I was considering, particularly in relation to my point regarding the potential connection with her decision to subsume her packmates. I was being coy before, but my thought there is that she might be pursuing an assimilation agenda, trying to become a greater being by incorporating others into herself. Her initial decision to merge with her peers might have been motivated by love, but it could have served as the inspiration for her interest in diablerie as a means to achieving perfection.<br /> <br /> I did have another thing I wanted to address, along the lines of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> saying &quot;no answer is right or wrong, as long as there's a story.&quot; When asked about the Discipline choices earlier, you mentioned how they were either chosen to support her Metamorphosist journey or as a means of remaining hidden. But there's one particular thing that doesn't (necessarily) seem to fit either of those categories: Presence. It doesn't seem like an obvious choice as a component of Metamorphosis, though I don't think it's impossible to make that case. It *definitely* doesn't fit with goal of remaining hidden, as Presence is all about being attention-grabbing. From a pragmatic perspective, Dominate would be better suited to the latter task, particularly if you reach the point of being able to alter memories. But to the extent that it does not (necessarily) fit either of those initial purposes, it has the potential to be viewed as an expression of a personal preference or desire that falls outside of her Metamorphosist goals, a possibility that could be interesting to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Presence can be used to not be noticed as well. It's a power for use on crowds while Dominate is geared more towards individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T20:13:28-07:00","id":1554886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1554885#post1554885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Presence can be used to not be noticed as well. It's a power for use on crowds while Dominate is geared more towards individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is not to argue if it can be used for a given task, is to build a story behind it. Justifying everything on pragmatism only makes for a less interesting character.<br /> <br /> And no, <b>Presence</b> can't be used to not be noticed. All its powers are about getting attention, it isn't simply <b>Dominate</b> for crowds, that's a common mistake, but a mistake nonetheless. Every single use of <b>Presence</b> will all but guarantee the victims won't ever forget you, and most powers will immediately attract the attention of everyone nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T10:29:05-07:00","id":1554895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1554885#post1554885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Presence can be used to not be noticed as well. It's a power for use on crowds while Dominate is geared more towards individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> kind of nails it above. There could be an argument for using Presence in an indirect manner to help with secrecy, by using it to create a cult-like web of devoted worshippers who will then do the grunt-work of helping you remain incognito. But Presence is absolutely not just an AoE version of Dominate. There are Presence powers designed for use on single targets, and the two Disciplines operate on different principles, with different limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T12:32:42-07:00","id":1554896,"title":"","content":"Well anyways a detail I left out was that just like how she has a twisted concept of love she also has a twisted concept of beauty which is why she has the set of delicate woman's arms from a Revenant she liked, she also has the elegant long neck of a noblewoman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T13:40:20-07:00","id":1554919,"title":"","content":"Presence is about making one more likeable and to stand out in the crowd by emotional manipulation. In some ways it's more unpredictable then Dominate in it use upon crowds and people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:18:22-08:00","id":1554963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547343-concept-for-an-npc?p=1554896#post1554896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well anyways a detail I left out was that just like how she has a twisted concept of love she also has a twisted concept of beauty which is why she has the set of delicate woman's arms from a Revenant she liked, she also has the elegant long neck of a noblewoman.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's totally workable as a concept, for sure. It's just something that needs to be considered when developing her character: there's a clash between wanting to stay hidden and wanting to stand out. If you want to try and keep both aspects as part of the character, you'll want to spend time figuring out how those contradictory desires play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T18:14:25-08:00","id":1554995,"title":"","content":"Well, it's more about staying hidden from the mundane world while presenting herself to other Kindred and her subordinates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}